NOTICE — third-party code and data used in this repository
===========================================================

This repository contains the MSCoSEA algorithm together with a slim copy of
the PlatEMO platform, ports of the baseline algorithms compared in the paper,
and third-party benchmark suites. All third-party components are listed below
with their origin. They remain the work of their respective authors and are
included solely for reproducibility of the published comparison.

Platform
--------
* PlatEMO — Tian, Y., Cheng, R., Zhang, X., Jin, Y., "PlatEMO: A MATLAB
  Platform for Evolutionary Multi-Objective Optimization [Educational Forum]",
  IEEE Computational Intelligence Magazine, 2017.
  The `PlatEMO/` folder of this repository is a slimmed copy of the platform
  (GUI and unrelated algorithm/problem packages removed).

Benchmark problems
------------------
* MMF suite (MMF1-MMF15 and variants) — standard multimodal multiobjective
  benchmarks; see Yue, C., Qu, B., Yu, K., Liang, J., Li, X., "A Novel Scalable
  Test Problem Suite for Multimodal Multiobjective Optimization", Swarm and
  Evolutionary Computation, 2019, and the PlatEMO distribution.
* IDMP suite (IDMPM*T*, IDMP*_e) — Liu, Y., Ishibuchi, H., Yen, G. G.,
  Nojima, Y., Masuyama, N., "Handling Imbalance Between Convergence and
  Diversity in the Decision Space in Evolutionary Multimodal Multiobjective
  Optimization", IEEE Transactions on Evolutionary Computation, 2020.
* NMMF suite (NMMF1-NMMF15) and its reference PS/PF data
  (`PlatEMO/Problems/Multi-objective optimization/HDMMF/NMMF*_Reference_PSPF_data.mat`)
  — from the authors of the suite above; mode partitions used in the paper are
  obtained by connectivity clustering of the published reference sets.
* Polygon problems (`Polygon_p`, parameterized) — introduced in the present
  paper.

